"pmid">10647931</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hedinger</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Sobin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><source>Histological typing of thyroid tumours. World Health Organization. International Histological Classification of Tumours</source><year>1988</year><publisher-name>Berlin: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name>2nd ed</citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hemmer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wasenius</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Knuutila</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Franssila</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Joensuu</surname></name><name><surname>H</surname></name></person-group><article-title>DNA copy number changes in thyroid carcinoma</article-title><source>Am J Pathol</source><year>1999</year><volume>154</volume><fpage>1539</fpage><lpage>1547</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Am J Pathol||154|1539||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10329606</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kallioniemi</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Kallioniemi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Piper</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Isolda</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldman</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinkel</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimizing comparative genomic hybridization for analysis of DNA sequence copy number changes in solid tumours</article-title><sour